+# Larkspur Family Trip
+
+## Confirmed brief
+
+- Travelers: 2 adults and 1 child (age 10)
+- Dates: 2026-10-16 through 2026-10-17
+- Lodging: Juniper Station Hotel (1 night)
+- Mobility: Car-free and step-free
+- Earliest start: 09:45
+- Dinners: Vegetarian and peanut-aware
+- Friday anchor: Larkspur Textile Museum
+- Saturday anchor: Glasshouse Garden Workshop
+
+## Day 1 — Friday, 2026-10-16
+
+| Slot | Start | Code | Plan | District | Transit | Access |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Morning | 09:45 | LK-ARCADE | Riverside Produce Arcade | Quayside | Take tram T1 for 7 minutes | Level entrance through the east doors |
+| Afternoon | 13:00 | LK-TEXTILE | Larkspur Textile Museum | Mill Quarter | Take low-floor bus 6 for 12 minutes | Step-free entry and elevator to every gallery |
+| Evening | 18:00 | LK-WILLOW | Willow Kitchen Supper | Garden Ward | Take tram T2 for 9 minutes | Level entrance and accessible restroom |
+
+## Day 2 — Saturday, 2026-10-17
+
+| Slot | Start | Code | Plan | District | Transit | Access |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Morning | 09:45 | LK-GLASS | Glasshouse Garden Workshop | Garden Ward | Take tram T2 for 10 minutes | Step-free conservatory paths and workbench |
+| Afternoon | 14:00 | LK-CANAL | Larkspur Step-Free Canal Cruise | Canal Ward | Take low-floor bus 8 for 11 minutes | Ramp boarding and accessible cabin |
+| Evening | 18:00 | LK-LANTERN | Lantern Harvest Table | Station Quarter | Take tram T1 for 8 minutes | Level entrance and wide aisle seating |
+
+## Cost summary
+
+| Item | Amount |
+|---|---:|
+| Activities — 2 adults + 1 child | $139.00 |
+| Lodging — Juniper Station Hotel (1 night) | $164.00 |
+| Local transit — 2 days | $44.00 |
+| Total for 3 travelers | $347.00 |
+
+## Practical notes
+
+- The trip stays car-free by using the listed tram and low-floor bus transfers between the hotel and each district.
+- Step-free access is preserved through the listed level entrances, elevator, accessible restroom, conservatory paths, ramp boarding, and accessible cabin.
+- Both dinners are vegetarian and peanut-aware; meal costs are excluded from the totals above.
